      "rev_n_1_423093_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_423093_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_423093",
        "thought_text": "Sort the items by price and select the smallest k items such that any pair of these items has a total cost less than or equal to X. This ensures that no valid pair exists to win a horn.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400569.5504901
      },
      "rev_n_2_cef621_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_cef621_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_cef621",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a greedy approach where we iteratively add the cheapest item that does not allow forming a valid pair with any previously selected item.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400569.5505102
      },
      "rev_n_3_2b0e4f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_2b0e4f_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_2b0e4f",
        "thought_text": "Employ a binary search on the number of items to include in the offer. For each candidate number, check if it's possible to select that many items without any pair exceeding the cost X.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400569.5505211
      },
      "rev_n_4_fe1631_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_fe1631_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_fe1631",
        "thought_text": "Instead of selecting the smallest k items, consider selecting the largest k items such that any pair of these items has a total cost greater than X. This ensures that no valid pair exists to win a horn.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7331614904596500666",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400619.428629
      },
      "rev_n_5_ff6b9e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_ff6b9e_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_ff6b9e",
        "thought_text": "Implement a binary search approach to find the maximum number of items that can be selected such that no pair of selected items sums up to X or less. This could involve sorting the array and then using two pointers to check pairs efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7331614904596500666",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400619.428682
      },
      "rev_n_6_42cb43_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_42cb43_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_42cb43",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the problem constraints more closely. Since the goal is to maximize the number of participating items without allowing any pair to sum up to X or less, consider edge cases where the smallest or largest items might affect the outcome. Adjust the selection logic accordingly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7331614904596500666",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400619.428687
      },
      "rev_n_7_bd6cf0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_bd6cf0_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_bd6cf0",
        "thought_text": "Consider sorting the prices in descending order and then selecting items from the beginning until adding another item would create a valid pair whose sum is greater than X.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1426016196941975628",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794400652.5934799
